    description: "Phase 5 (TDD). Walk all 'identifier_ref' descendants of each operator_definition/theorem/assumption. For each, resolver.lookup(name) against global registry. Skip self-references. Deduplicate with seen_ref_pairs: set[tuple[str, str]]. Edge type 'references', confidence 0.80. Key insight: identifier (declarations) vs identifier_ref (references) — the name child of operator_definition is 'identifier', so walking 'identifier_ref' descendants naturally excludes it. Parameter names and LET-bound names won't be in registry so are skipped. Primed variables (x') parse as separate identifier_ref + prime nodes — no stripping needed. Write tests: test_operator_body_references, test_no_self_reference, test_deduplication. Ref: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/tla_plan.md §Edge Extraction, §Reference extraction logic, §Primed variables"  # 2863
